NETWORKING COMMANDS - INTERVIEW POV
----------

## IP & Interface Commands

| Command        | Purpose                                      |
|---------------|----------------------------------------------|
| ip addr       | Show IP address & interface details          |
| ifconfig      | Show IP address (old command)                |
| ip link       | Show network interface status                |
| hostname -I   | Show system IP address only                  |

---

## Connectivity Commands

| Command      | Purpose                          |
|-------------|----------------------------------|
| ping        | Check host connectivity          |
| traceroute  | Show path to destination         |
| tracepath   | Similar to traceroute            |

---

## DNS Commands

| Command    | Purpose                         |
|-----------|---------------------------------|
| nslookup  | Domain → IP resolution          |
| dig       | Detailed DNS information        |
| host      | Quick DNS lookup                |

---

##Port Checking Commands

| Command        | Purpose                              |
|---------------|--------------------------------------|
| ss -tuln      | Show open TCP/UDP ports              |
| netstat -tuln | Show open ports (old command)        |
| lsof -i       | Show processes using ports           |
| nc -zv        | Test port connectivity               |
| telnet        | Test remote port connectivity        |

---

## Routing Commands

| Command   | Purpose                     |
|----------|-----------------------------|
| ip route | Show routing table          |
| route -n | Show routing table (old)    |

---

## Remote Access Commands

| Command | Purpose                  |
|--------|--------------------------|
| ssh    | Secure remote login      |
| scp    | Copy files remotely      |
| sftp   | Secure file transfer     |

